===A7_S3_D2===
Narrator: After chatting about the shipment, the topic goes back to your boat, which you’ve managed to roughly patch up.
Saorise: With any luck, we can use it to transport goods to the beach closer to the mountain trail. It’ll save us a lot of work once the packing gets tough. #portrait:Saorise
Saorise: But enough about business. You wanted to know more about Noah’s history, didn’t you? #portrait:Saorise
Noelle: Well… just about what hideouts he might’ve had. I suppose you could say that my curiosity is just due to a gut feeling. #portrait:NoelleUm
Narrator: Saorise chuckles. 
Saorise: Said gut feeling is what saves our lives at sea. You should be more confident in your instincts. #portrait:Saorise
Narrator: She explains that Noah did indeed use a cave off the beach as a base, but it’s been caved in over the past centuries. 
Saorise: It may take a while to find an entrance, or a safe one, at that. #portrait:Saorise
Noelle: I see… #portrait:NoelleSad
Noelle: This isn’t related to Noah, but… #portrait:NoelleUm
Noelle: I’ve been meaning to ask — did anyone on Thavmia regard the Krakenfolk as strange or… monstrous, at first? #portrait:NoelleUm
Noelle: I mean! Surely it must’ve been a shock to the first person who transformed. #portrait:NoelleSad
Noelle: (I hope she understands what I mean. I’m not trying to say that the Krakenfolk or other Thavma are strange by any means…) #portrait:NoelleUm
Saorise: Well… of course they did. #portrait:Saorise
Saorise: Some even went as far to say that it was the Great Disaster’s curse on mankind, for the acts Noah committed. #portrait:Saorise
Saorise: But… after a bit of time, we calmed down and learned to understand and adapt. #portrait:Saorise
Saorise: The main belief that we uphold, is that this is simply another biological effect — this time, from the Kraken’s blood, rather than Thavmia’s unique landscape. With a few extraordinary abilities to boot! #portrait:Saorise
Saorise: To be honest, it connected us to some other islands, who traveled here after they experienced transformations, in hopes that we might have an answer or cure. #portrait:Saorise
Saorise: After all, Thavmia is known to some others as a place of miracles. A story, in some sense, for as long as we only existed in their minds. #portrait:Saorise
Saorise: Your home is not the only one to regard Krakenfolk as strange. However, their lack of creatures is another ‘strange’ trait as well! #portrait:Saorise
Saorise: I suppose that just goes to show that you can never be truly done learning about the world. #portrait:Saorise
+ [But…]
-> choicea7
+ [About the weather…]
-> choicea7

===choicea7===
Noelle: Both the human settlement and Ichthyos have been worried about it… #portrait:NoelleUm
Narrator: The past few days have been sunny and bright, but…
Noelle: If the weather worsens, will the regular evacuations be— #portrait:NoelleUm
Narrator: Saorise turns towards the ocean, gaze narrowing.
Narrator: Not a moment too soon, you too feel a change in the air — the wind is picking up, and if you crane your ears…
Ada: It’s a storm! #portrait:Ada
Narrator: You nod to Saorise, running off to grab Amelia and haul your tent further inland.
Saorise: Everyone, get indoors! Do not go outside until I say so! #portrait:Saorise
Narrator: Frowns and whispers pass. The water levels pinch and shove the beach.
Narrator: <i>’Could it be…’</i> 
Narrator: <i>’Have the floods started early?’</i> 
-> DONE